  "result": "All tests pass! I've successfully implemented line discounts for the invoicing system. Here's what was added:\n\n**Key changes:**\n\n1. **Error handling** - Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error code for invalid discount percentages\n\n2. **Line discounts** - Lines now support an optional `discountPercent` field (0-100, with decimals allowed):\n   - `createInvoice` and `addLine` accept and validate `discountPercent`\n   - Defaults to 0 if not provided\n   - Returns `DISCOUNT_INVALID` if not a number or outside 0-100 range\n\n3. **New `lineDiscount()` function** - Calculates discount on a single line:\n   - Formula: lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent / 100\n   - Results rounded to whole cents using `roundCents()`\n   - Clamped at 0 to ensure non-negative amounts\n\n4. **Updated `invoiceTotals()`** - Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }`:\n   - `subtotal` = sum of all line totals (unchanged)\n   - `discount` = sum of all line discounts\n   - `total` = subtotal - discount, clamped at 0 (no negative totals)\n\n5. **Comprehensive tests** - Added 20 new tests covering:\n   - Valid discounts and edge cases (0, decimals, 100)\n   - Invalid discounts (non-numbers, out of range)\n   - Discount calculations with rounding\n   - Multiple lines with different discounts\n   - Total clamping when discount exceeds subtotal\n   - Both `createInvoice` and `addLine` discount handling\n\nAll 95 tests pass, including the original 75 tests from previous requests.",
